===Mastery Strategies===
{{MastComp|{{MastStrat|first|Active|-60}}|{{MastStrat|second|Machine}}|{{MastStrat|third|Collect and use}}|{{MastStrat|fourth|Encounter Blackouts}}|{{MastStrat|fifth|Encounter Twisteds}}|{{MastStrat|sixth|Meters|2Star}}}}
==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up Research Capsules and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more [[Ichor]].
*For the second requirement, have a Distractor Toon bring {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} to the elevator to you so you can get aggro. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting Research faster because of his Passive Ability. This will be easier if Twisted Vee is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*For the third requirement, play as {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} and try to complete her Mastery Quests by going on multiple runs. It is recommended to go on an organized Run or do specific quests in certain runs.

==Strategies==
Vee is one of the best extractors in the game (only being outclassed by {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}} and {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}), having 4{{Star}} [[Skill Check]] and 5 Star [[Extraction Speed]], making her optimal for those who desire to grind for {{TI|Ichor|name=true}} or simply just want to extract [[Machines]] with ease. However, those powered [[Stats]] come at the cost of being one of the worst at escaping [[Twisteds]], as she possesses below-average Stealth and below-average mobility.

As a slow Toon with subpar survivability, Vee requires some support for it, whether it's from other Toons, [[Trinkets]], or [[Items]]. With that being said, keeping {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=false|plural=a}}, {{II|Smoke Bomb|name=false}}s, and {{II|Bandage|name=false}}s in your inventory when playing as her can be extremely helpful, and having support Toons like {{CI|Astro|name=true}} or {{CI|Tisha|name=true}} around is even better when trying to get to places and [[Machines]] that are much farther from the [[Elevator]].

If on a solo or alone, Vee will require assistance from other sources, and have to pay attention to her surroundings in order to not have an unpleasant encounter with any dangerous Twisteds that she struggles to outrun. With that being said, it's best to keep in mind that [[Stamina]] management is important. Only use Stamina when Twisteds are around, and save up to 60 Stamina in the case of being noticed by one or more Twisteds ever happens. You should also be aware of your Stealth in such scenarios.

Some of Vee's best qualities and benefits come in the form of her [[Abilities]]. Vee's Active Ability, {{AI|Vee|name=true}}, serves many purposes, being helpful for both distractors and extractors alike. Her Ability shows the location of all Twisteds and Machines on the map, allowing distractors to locate and gather Twisteds easier, and allowing extractors to locate Machines more efficiently. In terms of usage, Mic Check doesn't really need to be saved for specific times, considering it will be beneficial to all whenever you use it, though it can be slightly better utilized at the start of a [[Floor]]. Alongside her Active, Vee has a much similar Passive Ability, that being '''Camera Hijack''', which highlights two Machines that are nearest to her location. Although seemingly being a worse version of her Active Ability, it can be helpful at times where her Ability is on cooldown. It also helps her locate Machines before anyone else in her team does (this is important considering Vee's lower mobility would hinder her locating Machines faster), or even locate Machines for her teammates at times when her Ability is on cooldown. Both of her Abilities can allow her to point stealthier extractors to more open Machines, or higher mobility extractors to Machines far from the elevator, enabling her to keep out of the way of distractors or just general danger, while still contributing to overall extraction indirectly. Do note that Duo Machines will only be highlighted with a white outline (meaning they're being extracted) if a Toon is extracting on the left attachment, so you may have to look for the [[Ichor]] inside the Machine to see if it's being filled, if only the right attachment is being extracted from.

Another small upside to Vee is her light-production during [[Blackouts]]. Though it isn't much, Vee will produce a light during such event, which helps her see better during Blackouts. She can also use this light radius to guide other teammates, though due to her low speed, this may not be the safest strategy.

Overall, Vee is a great support and extractor Toon, though has both downsides and upsides. Additionally, playing as her requires carefulness and attention to your surroundings, so it's best to train your senses before trying to play as her during planned or serious runs. She requires patience and can punish reckless traversal, though her {{AI|Vee|name=true}} can be extremely helpful in gathering information about the floor.

===Trinket Combinations===
