==Trivia==
===Lore===
*Vee's [[Toon Handler]] is {{CI|Veronica Hurley|name=true}}.
*Vee is the host of a quiz show. Said quiz show is implied to be popular among [[Toons]], with some even competing in them. The game show is also quite popular to the kids, with some Episodes dedicated to her quiz show.
*Vee's designation is M-005 with the '''M''' most likely standing for {{Type|Main}}.
*Vee seems to be unhappy that {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} keeps winning all her game show prizes, as seen in the [[:File:Vee, Scraps and Brightney TV Animation|Vee, Scraps, and Brightney TV Animation]] and their interactions together.
*Vee most likely hides any other emotions she is feeling by keeping up her sarcastic and superiority personality. This is suggested in an interaction with {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}, where she gets defensive when Cosmo was told by {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} that she hasn't been feeling the best.
*Vee seems to have a mutual dislike of {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}, and this is further implied in one of her interactions with {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} where she says that she tries to argue with Dandy. Further proof of her negative attitude towards Dandy is in one of her finishing extraction lines, "I bet Dandy couldn't do this!". There are also many things that further prove this, such as:
**Dandy's dialogue when buying Vee: "{{Text|Oh… Vee.}}";
**In [[Dandy's Store]], during the [[Easter Event]], Vee's themed Easter egg is seen in the garbage bin;
**In [[Vee's Floor]], where a small Dandy Plush is seen in a garbage can in one of the side rooms backstage;
**In the [[Gift Shop]] map, Vee's cutout is knocked down on the floor, but Dandy's is still standing up;
**Dandy makes fun of her for thinking she can be more popular than him in his [[Gossip]] about her;
**{{CI|Dyle|name=true}} reveals that Dandy decries Vee while talking to him in his Gossip, even explicitly stating "he does not enjoy her company", emphasizing the mutual resentment.
**A couple official (non-canon) doodles reflect this dynamic. Vee talks herself up while punching down Dandy in front of him, as Dandy from afar tells {{CI|Astro|name=true}} "I want to kill her".
**Vee's rivalry with Dandy and Sprout (two plant-based [[Toons]]) could overall be a reference to the "Nature vs Technology" trope.
*Vee has trouble complimenting others without it coming off as backhanded, as shown in one of her Interactions with {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1254149700878336122</ref>
*{{CI|Delilah|name=true}} and {{CI|Arthur|name=true}} had plans to upgrade Vee to Vee Version 2, but it's likely this never happened due to [[Gardenview]] closing down before Vee was upgraded.
**If a player plays as Vee and gets close to the monitor that plays the very clip proving this statement, she will respond with "{{Text|. . .|Vee}}".
***This makes it the first [[Floor]]-based interaction, where [[Toons]] speak without Active [[Ability]] usage, [[Machine]] completion, or being in the [[Elevator]].
*Vee appears to show an interest towards {{CI|Blot|name=true}}. In one of her interactions with him, she asks him if he'd rather keep performing for his troupe, implying that she's possibly offering him to work with her. She even insists somewhat after he turned her down.
**She's not, however, interested in him as a Circus Troupe member, as in her second interaction with him, she firmly shuts down the idea of having the troupe perform during one of her shows.
*It is possible that because Vee is both a [[Main Character]] and the TV show host of a famous gameshow, {{CI|Glisten|name=true}} is envious of all the attention Vee gets and tries to compete with Vee and her gameshow, or Glisten genuinely admires Vee and wants to become a gameshow host like her, or possibly even some mix of both. Based on their interactions, they also seem to know each other in some way.
**Vee also says that Glisten, in one of their interactions, "couldn't make a good game show, even if he tried," possibly hinting at Glisten mentioning wanting to have a gameshow before. However, this might be Vee reprimanding Glisten for his egotistical personality.
***The two also appear in a cartoon together, talking in a backstage area.
*Vee runs on batteries, as seen in the "Don't forget to recharge!" short, with Vee losing power on her batteries and [[Brightney|{{CI|Brightney|name=true}}]] bringing batteries to recharge her.
**This was implied a bit earlier in the "The Vee Virus" [[poster]], where Brightney is seen with batteries, likely to fix her.
===General===
*Vee's name is derived from the pronunciation of TV (Tee''Vee'').
*Vee's full name was revealed in an 11/14/2024 QnA stream.
*When hit, Vee's face changes to a blue "Rebooting" screen. Furthermore, her hurt face shows a different screen depending on which [[Skin]] she's wearing.
**When using the {{Skin|Vintage}} Skin, a black and white screen with the words "The End" appears.
**When using the {{Skin|Cosmic Signal}} Skin, it changes to a blue screen with the text "Signal Error" next to a signal tower symbol.
**{{Skin|Star-Time Vee}}'s hurt face changes to a black screen with "Please Wait…", a crescent moon, a line in the middle, and two X's; one above the line and one below.
**When using the {{Skin|Show-Time}} Skin, the screen changes to a black screen with an eye and the text "Are You Entertained".
**Using her {{Skin|Zapped Creation}} Skin displays a symbol on her screen similar to the {{CDI|Electrician|name=true}} [[Card]], with the word "DANGER" at the top and "HIGH VOLTAGE" at the bottom.
**{{Skin|Holiday Special}} shows a Christmas tree with presents around it.
**{{Skin|Vee-ster Bunny}} shows a picture of a pink rabbit facing the front.
*Vee is one of the characters that glows a different color during [[Blackouts]], with the other five being [[Astro]], {{CI|Connie|name=true}}, {{CI|Rudie|name=true}}, {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}, and {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}.
*Vee used to only have 2{{Star}} in [[Stamina]]; however, it was changed to 3 Stars in [[Changelog|v0.2]].
*Vee is currently the only [[Toon]] to have a custom font in her chatbox, that being the "[https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Press+Start+2P Press Start 2P]" font.
*Vee was the second [[Toon]] to have an [[easter egg]] in another game not owned by [[BlushCrunch]], able to be found in [[w:c:piggy|Piggy]]. You could find her on a monitor in the lobby of the [[w:c:piggy:Decay|Decay]] chapter, with the previous character with an Easter egg being {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}, who has an available morph in [https://www.roblox.com/games/15025355743/SBRP?gameSetTypeId=100000003&homePageSessionInfo=e19e5d0d-c3db-494a-9173-e36054d9f4d5&isAd=false&numberOfLoadedTiles=46&page=sortDetailPageHome&placeId=15025355743&position=28&universeId=5174194165 Storybook Roleplay], with the Bin Codes being /mbin2162 respectively.
*Vee's favorite contestant is [[Brightney|{{CI|Brightney|name=true}}]], as seen from their dialogues and confirmed by [[Qwel]] during the 2025 New Years stream.
*Vee's microphone used to be stored inside her torso when not in use. However, as of [[Changelog|v0.9.1]], this has since changed as with her updated model, her microphone is now stored inside her head.
*[[Qwel]] confirmed in the New Year QnA Stream that both Vee and [[Rodger]] don't have mouths and don't need to eat, but they both can eat the food items because of gameplay reasons.
*Vee hints some parts of her [[statistics]] in one of her interactions with [[Astro]].
**When she says "Or if you need to have a [[Machine]] done faster!", she refers to her having high extraction rates with 4 Star [[Skill Check]] and 5 Star [[Extraction Speed]] compared to Astro's 2 Star Skill Check and 3 Star Extraction Speed, defining that she is a regular extractor and a sort of supporter for Astro.
**When she says, "OR if a [[Twisted]] tries anything!" this could be a reference to her 2 Star [[Stealth]] and Astro's 5 Star Stealth with Vee being able to take Twisteds off him to protect him, acting as a semi-distractor for Astro, despite the fact she isn't a regular distractor due to her below average Movement Speed stat.
*Vee used to be the Main (and [[Toon]] in general) with the most extractability in the game if not counting [[Dandy]] and [[Dyle]], having 4 Star Skill Check and 5 Star Extraction Speed. She was later dethroned by {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}} and [[Soulvester|{{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}]], topping her with 5 Stars in both Skill Check and Extraction Speed.
**However, since they are both {{HT|Halloween}} exclusive, she still has the best extraction stats out of the year-round Toons.
*Prior to [[Changelog|v0.26.1]], Vee and [[Scraps]] had the longest interaction in the game, with 7 lines.
**This dialogue is now the second-longest, with the longest ones being [[Brusha]]'s dialogues with [[Rodger]] and {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}, with 8 lines each.
*Vee is mistakenly referred to with they/them pronouns in her [[Ability]]'s description.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1330900639366250608</ref>
*Vee is the third [[Main Character]] [[Toon]] to have their own [[Floor]] (not counting [[Holiday Floors]]), after [[Astro]] and [[Shelly]].
*Vee's remodel gave both her Toon and {{CI|Twisted Vee}}[[Twisted Vee|Twisted counterpart]] a static overlay on her screen, making her more like a TV.
*Vee is the first [[Main]] [[Toon]] and the first Toon in general to get two [[Gamepass]] [[Skins]].
*Vee's [[Show-Time]] [[Skin]] seems to be based on an [[Unused Content#Red_Vee|unused]] Vee skin concept which also had a white screen and red as the main color.
*Before [[Changelog|v0.10.1]], Vee's {{AI|Vee|name=true}} cooldown was 60 seconds. This was reduced to 50.
**Additionally, her Camera Hijack ability was buffed, now highlighting 2 [[Machines]] rather than 1.
**'''Mic Check''' got a further buff in v0.13.1, now highlighting all Machines alongside [[Twisteds]].
*Vee is the second [[Toon]] to use one hand to extract, the first being [[Cosmo]] and the third being [[Razzle & Dazzle]].
*Whenever a [[Machine]] is highlighted by her [[Abilities]], if its status changes (like if a Toon leaves a Machine), the highlight doesn't change until it reactivates/glows again.
*Vee is one of the first 3 [[Main Characters]] to be added, along with [[Astro]] and [[Pebble]]. She is the only female to do so.
*Weirdly, a [[Duo Machine]] is considered occupied by Vee's [[Abilities]] only when someone is extracting the left side.

